.\" Manpage for javars (the `java` binary).
.\" Contact https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/javars to correct errors or omissions.
.TH JAVA 1 "2026-08-30" "javars 0.1.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
java \- Java on fusevm, a Java frontend lowered to bytecode and run on a Cranelift JIT (no JVM)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B java
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE.java\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B java
\fB\-\-lsp\fR | \fB\-\-dap\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B javars
lexes and parses Java source and lowers it to
.B fusevm
bytecode executed on a three\-tier Cranelift JIT \(em the same shared engine
behind
.BR zshrs ,
.BR stryke ,
.BR awkrs ,
elisp, and ruby. There is no bespoke VM and no JVM; execution and codegen live
in fusevm, and there are no
.I .class
files.
.PP
The current slice runs a single entry class: javars locates
.B public static void main(String[] args)
in the given file and executes its body. Statements cover local declarations,
assignment and compound assignment, C\-style
.BR if / while / for ,
.BR break / continue ,
post\-increment/decrement, and
.BR System.out.print / println .
Java's
.B +
is string concatenation when either operand is a
.BR String .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-version
Print the version banner and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-help ", " \-?
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
Print the lexer token stream for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Print the parsed AST for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tiers
Run it, then report which fusevm execution tier took each of its chunks.
.TP
.B \-\-disasm
Print a fusevm bytecode disassembly listing for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-lsp
Speak the Language Server Protocol over stdio (completion, hover, and
diagnostics from the same parser the runtime uses).
.TP
.B \-\-dap
Speak the Debug Adapter Protocol over stdio (breakpoints, single\-stepping, and
local\-variable inspection over the running program).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B java
exits 0 on success and 1 on a lex/parse/compile error or an I/O failure. Errors
are written to standard error in the terse form
.IR "java: <reason>" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a program:
.RS 4
.EX
java Hello.java
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inspect the lowered bytecode:
.RS 4
.EX
java \-\-disasm Fib.java
.EE
.RE
.PP
Debug a program from an editor (DAP over stdio):
.RS 4
.EX
java \-\-dap
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR javaall (1),
.BR java (1)
(the reference JDK launcher).
The comprehensive javars reference is
.BR javaall (1).
